<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bernt Notke</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1440–1509</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bernt Notke was a painter and sculptor based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lubeck">Lübeck</a>, the leading artist of the Baltic region in the late 15th century. His works include the Danse Macabre now in St Nicholas' Church in Tallinn (Reval), the high altar of Tallinn's Church of the Holy Spirit and the monumental Saint George and the Dragon in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stockholm">Stockholm</a> Cathedral.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bernt-notke.jpg" alt="Bernt Notke" width="122" height="174" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernt Notke · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bernt_Notke_goss_74a.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
